<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="dimorphecolate biosynthesis" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260304101735">
  <Description>&lt;i&gt;Supporting evidence for this pathway in Oryza sativa Japonica Group&lt;/i&gt;: Enzyme(s) that catalyzes one or more of the key reactions in this pathway were predicted in Oryza sativa Japonica Group. &lt;A href=&quot;http://www.plantcyc.org/about/savi_pipeline&quot;&gt;[more info]&lt;/A&gt; &lt;i&gt;Summary from MetaCyc:&lt;/i&gt; |FRAME: CPD-8204 Dimorphecolate| (9-OH-18:2&amp;Delta;10trans,12trans) is the major fatty acid found in seeds of |FRAME: TAX-13490| species. It is a conjugated fatty acid that has three unusual structural features: 1) a C-9 hydroxyl group 2) conjugated &amp;Delta;10,&amp;Delta;12 double bonds, and 3) two &lt;i&gt;trans&lt;/i&gt; double bonds, rather than the much more common &lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt; bonds. This special fatty acid has potential values in industrial applications such as the manufacture of paints, inks, lubricants, plastics, and nylon. |FRAME: CPD-8204 Dimorphecolate| is derived from |FRAME: OLEATE-CPD| by the concerted activity of two desaturase enzymes, encoded by the |FRAME: G-9662| and |FRAME: G-9663| genes |CITS: [14718523]|. cDNAs of both enzymes have been cloned. Ectopic expression in yeast and soybean somatic embryo cells demonstrated that |FRAME: G-9662| encodes a oleate 12(&lt;i&gt;E&lt;/i&gt;)-desaturase, able to convert |FRAME: OLEATE-CPD| (18:1&amp;Delta;9cis) to |FRAME: CPD-8203| (18:2&amp;Delta;9cis,12trans). The ectopic expression experiments also demonstrated that |FRAME: G-9663| encodes a &amp;Delta;9 fatty acid conjugase-like enzyme that is able to introduce a hydroxyl group at C9 while simultaneously converting the &lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt; &amp;Delta;9 double bond to a &lt;i&gt;trans&lt;/i&gt; &amp;Delta;10 double bond |CITS: [14718523]|.</Description>
  <Authors>
